&lt;p&gt;We operate and maintain several facilities, including: one 1K-8T STM-AFM, two MBE systems, one RT AFM-MFM system.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="stmafm"&gt;STM/AFM&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;figure class="align-center justify-caption"&gt;
&lt;img loading="lazy" src="https://dfwanguh.github.io/images/instrumentation/Quanta.jpg#center"
alt="This is a customer design STM with 1.2 K lowest temperature and 8 T magnetic field. It also capable of surface magnetism imaging with SP-STM mode as well as molecular bonds imaging with nc-AFM mode. Beside, two HF lines arrive at the tunneling junction with MW frequency larger than 20 GHz." width="800"/&gt; &lt;figcaption&gt;
Quanta&lt;p&gt;This is a customer design STM with 1.2 K lowest temperature and 8 T magnetic field. It also capable of surface magnetism imaging with SP-STM mode as well as molecular bonds imaging with nc-AFM mode. Beside, two HF lines arrive at the tunneling junction with MW frequency larger than 20 GHz.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Join Us</title><link>https://dfwanguh.github.io/join/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://dfwanguh.github.io/join/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;We are always looking for motivated students interested in scanning probe microscopy and surface physics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please send your CV to: &lt;strong&gt;dfwang AT bit.edu.cn&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Publications</title><link>https://dfwanguh.github.io/publications/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://dfwanguh.github.io/publications/</guid><description>&lt;div style="text-align: justify;"&gt;
&lt;h2 id="2026"&gt;2026&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Katerina Vaxevani, Jon Ortuzar, Stefano Trivini, Georg Monninger, Dongfei Wang, Lucía Gómez-Rodrigo, Diego Peña, Jose Ignacio Pascual.&lt;br&gt;
&amp;ldquo;Parity-dependent coupling of molecular spin chains to a superconductor&amp;rdquo;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;em&gt;arXiv:2608.22736, 2026&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dongfei Wang, Wenbin Li, Eric Mascot, Roland Wiesendanger.&lt;br&gt;
&amp;ldquo;Exchange-induced suppression of superconductivity in a nano-skyrmion lattice-superconductor hybrid&amp;rdquo;.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;em&gt;arXiv:2608.09207, 2026&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dongfei Wang, Jon Ortuzar, Freek Massee, Ruidan Zhong, Genda Gu, Wende Xiao, Yugui Yao, Roland Wiesendanger.&lt;br&gt;
&amp;ldquo;Distinguishing Majorana zero modes from trivial defect states on the surface of the iron-based superconductor Fe (Te, Se)&amp;rdquo;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Communications Physics, 2026&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Research</title><link>https://dfwanguh.github.io/research/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://dfwanguh.github.io/research/</guid><description>&lt;div style="text-align: justify;"&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;h2 id="majorana-physics-in-superconductors"&gt;Majorana Physics in superconductors&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Topological superconductors, as an emergent class of superconducting states, provides an ideal platform for the investigation of topology as well as parity symmetry. They also support the existence of Majorana anyons, quasiparticles that are their own antiparticles, with potential applications in fault-tolerant quantum computation. Low temperature STM/STS are advanced experimental techniques widely used to study topological superconducting states due to their ultrahigh spatial and energy resolution. Our research is focusing on using advanced STM technique, such as Spin-polarized STM, to image the magnetic field response of such anyons in topological superconductor candidates. Further more, we seek the possibility to manipulates Majorana anyons and make fusions with them.
This research is supported by the National Science Foundation of China.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Team</title><link>https://dfwanguh.github.io/team/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://dfwanguh.github.io/team/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="principal-investigator"&gt;Principal Investigator&lt;/h2&gt;
